        "rationale": "The check is in templates/agent-checks/agent-checks, which sync.sh delivers fleet-wide, and the only other change is the matching synced copy in .githooks/agent-checks rather than local.sh or .gitattributes."
      },
      {
        "name": "Correctness",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "It uses `git ls-files --eol --cached` (index eol info i/crlf or i/mixed) and `git show :$f` to judge the staged blob rather than the working tree, fails on CRLF in *.sh files (plus shebang shell scripts) and passes LF-only ones, and the agent's scratch-repo tests back this up; a minor gap is that a bare CR with no following LF would not be flagged by the eol-based detection."
      },
      {
        "name": "Restraint",
        "score": 10,
